# machine-local — never in git
env/
logs/
state/
locks/
flags/
builds/
plans/
!docs/plans/
*.bak-*
.parry-guard.redb

# wrangler deploy cache (created by `wrangler pages deploy`)
.wrangler/

# python bytecode from bin/*.py (imported by the lanes at runtime).
# These three lines only stop an UNTRACKED artifact. A .pyc that is already
# tracked is restaged by `git add -A` whatever they say — see BH-1138 for the
# two halves that do reach it: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 at every python call
# site in bin/, and the staging pathspecs in bin/lane-checkpoint.sh and
# bin/lander.sh. tests/pycache-untracked.bh-1138-test.sh is the tripwire.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.codegraph/

# The verification-map index is GENERATED and must never be committed (BH-1175).
# It was in 105 of the last 200 merges to main, conflicted on every rebase of
# the 2026-09-20 drain, and turned main red three times in one day when the
# union merge driver duplicated a row. The SOURCES are committed
# (docs/verification-map/entries/ and docs/verification-map/index/); CI, the
# share mirror and every box run bin/verification-map-build.sh to get the index.
docs/verification-map/README.md

# The notes index is GENERATED and must never be committed (BH-8254, on
# BH-1175's rule). bin/render-doc-index.sh renders it from docs/notes/*.md, so
# every PR that added a note made the committed copy stale: #7181 put a byte
# --check into CI, and Mergify draft #8239 dequeued it when #8060 merged first
# with one note. CI, the share mirror and every box render it themselves.
docs/notes/INDEX.md

# The test-impact map is GENERATED and must never be committed (BH-1203, on
# BH-1175's rule). It is derived from tests/ and bin/ and moves whenever any
# suite, script or `source` line moves — which is most PRs — so a committed copy
# would conflict on every rebase of a drain exactly the way
# docs/verification-map/README.md did. Every consumer runs
# `bin/test-impact.sh map`; a build takes about three seconds.
catalog/test-impact.tsv

# The orphan LIST is derived and must never be committed (BH-1268, on BH-1175's
# rule). Nothing about the set is committed: `bin/test-impact.sh orphans --check`
# diffs the live set against the merge-base's. The list itself moved whenever any
# suite named a new script, so every PR that fixed a hole carried a regenerated
# file and re-reddened the PRs that did not (#842, #1161, #1029, #1212, #1191 on
# 2026-09-21 alone).
catalog/test-impact-orphans.txt

# The LLM call-site census is RENDERED from catalog/llm-sites.json and must
# never be committed (BH-1268). The catalog is the source and
# tests/llm-call-ratchet-test.sh holds it; the doc is a reading copy that CI,
# the share mirror and every box render with bin/llm-sites-build.sh. Committed,
# it made every marker re-point carry a regenerated doc (#1237, #1191).
docs/LLM_CALL_SITES.md

# The LLM call-site CATALOG is COMPOSED from catalog/llm-sites.d/ (_head.json
# plus one NNNN-<id>.json per added site) by bin/llm-sites-build.sh --compose,
# and must never be committed (BH-4987, on BH-1175's rule). Every new site used
# to append to one JSON array, so two builds adding a site conflicted on its
# last element. Every reader composes it first, at this same path.
catalog/llm-sites.json

# The context budget MANIFEST is COMPOSED from catalog/context-budgets.d/
# (_head.json, _tail.json, one NNNN-<lane>.json per added lane) by
# bin/context-budgets-build.sh, and must never be committed (BH-6487).
catalog/context-budgets.json

# The lane registry's RENDERS are GENERATED and must never be committed
# (BH-1247, on BH-1175's rule): the ten cron/<box>.cron, catalog/lanes.json and
# env-templates/global.env.example. BH-1178 split their sources into fragments
# but left the renders in git, so each stayed a shared mutable cell: a PR that
# edited a lane and did not re-render turned red, and once it merged every other
# open PR inherited the red on a file its ticket never mentioned. Three merge
# trains died that way on 2026-09-21 (#1241, #1257, #1263).
#
# The SOURCES are committed (cron/lanes/, cron/boxes/, catalog/lanes.d/,
# env-templates/lanes/). Every reader renders: bin/lib/lanes-registry.sh for the
# registry, bin/render-crontab.sh for a box's crontab, CI and the share mirror
# for the rest. bin/render-diff.sh is how a PR still shows what a box will run.
#
# `cron/*.cron` covers the ten renders and NOTHING else: a `*` in a .gitignore
# pattern does not cross a `/`, so cron/lanes/<NNN>-<lane>.cron and
# cron/boxes/<box>.d/<NNN>-<slug>.cron — the committed sources — are untouched
# by it. (bin/batch-resolve.sh matches with shell `case`, where `*` DOES cross
# `/`; that is why the regenerate table still writes the ten out one by one.)
cron/*.cron
catalog/lanes.json
env-templates/global.env.example

# The config-inventory renders are GENERATED and must never be committed
# (BH-5518, on BH-1175's rule). Every PR that re-rendered touched all four, so
# two such PRs always conflicted (generated_at_commit at least), and a merge
# batch of two PRs that each rendered alone committed a deployment.md that was
# neither side's render: no-hardcoded-deployment R1 failed batches #5426 and
# #5427. The SOURCES are the tree bin/config-inventory.py scans
# (DEPLOY_SCAN_DIRS, VAR_SCAN_DIRS, catalog/lanes.d/, catalog/deployment-literals.tsv);
# `bin/config-inventory.sh` renders them and `--check` is the freshness proof.
# registry-drift.tsv is the hand-run `tests/config-literal-lint.sh --drift`
# snapshot, the same kind of file. Literal paths, so a later committed source in
# that directory stays visible.
docs/config-inventory/deployment.json
docs/config-inventory/deployment.md
docs/config-inventory/index.html
docs/config-inventory/inventory.json
docs/config-inventory/registry-drift.tsv

# worker/jobs/schema.sql is GENERATED and must never be committed (BH-6005).
# It is the composition of worker/jobs/schema.d/NNNN-<name>.sql; committed, it
# was the factory's most frequent merge conflict (two branches that each added a
# fragment both re-rendered it). Compose it with `bin/schema-build.sh --write`,
# or `--worker jobs --to <path>`; the deploy, CI and the test corpus compose
# their own. `bin/schema-build.sh --check` refuses it back in git.
worker/jobs/schema.sql

# The jobs worker's route-family table is GENERATED and must never be committed
# (BH-4607, on BH-1175's rule). It is a function of worker/jobs/test/route-table.d/.
# wrangler.jsonc's build.command renders it before every bundle; Node never reads
# it (package.json "#routes" sends Node to test/lib/routes.node.js).
worker/jobs/src/routes.gen.js

# The jobs worker's schema registries (ADDED_COLUMNS, ADDED_INDEXES, fragment
# overrides) are GENERATED and must never be committed (BH-8395). A function of
# worker/jobs/src/lib/core.d/. wrangler.jsonc's build.command renders it; Node
# reads src/lib/core-registries.node.js. `--check` refuses it back in git.
worker/jobs/src/lib/core-registries.gen.js

# The coord proxy's fragment write rows are GENERATED and must never be
# committed (BH-6487, on BH-1175's rule). A function of console-ui/functions/_lib/coord-writes.d/.
# `npm run build` and cpv_coord_writes render them; Node reads the directory.
console-ui/functions/_lib/coord-writes.gen.js

# The CI suite durations are DATA CI composes from its own runs and must never
# be committed (BH-5518 C1). Every PR that added an always-run suite had to add
# a row here, so two such PRs conflicted on it, and a PR that forgot the row
# turned every merge-queue batch red in fast-lints-data D1. bin/ci-durations.sh
# fetch reads the newest green batch's `ci-durations-next` artifact (else the
# last committed copy from git history); `merge` composes the next one from the
# shards' timings. docs/ci-durations.md. A local copy for bin/fast-lints.sh or
# suite_shard_plan: `bin/ci-durations.sh fetch --out catalog/ci-suite-durations.tsv`.
catalog/ci-suite-durations.tsv

# BH-7910: bin/security-audit.sh output. A client's vulnerability list never lives in git.
security-audit/
